Best Waterproof Socks of 2026

Versatile, durable and waterproof socks for hiking, running, and biking

October 9th, 2026, updated with a new best for hiking and new winner for best for cold weatherHome > Gear Reviews > Apparel

Wet feet can turn an otherwise great hike, ride, or run into a miserable day. Waterproof socks add another barrier between your feet and rain, puddles, wet trails, and water that makes its way past your shoes, while still allowing more breathability than an improvised plastic barrier.

I tested waterproof socks while hiking, biking, running, and walking in wet Midwest conditions, including muddy trails, steady rain, puddles, and long rides in bad weather. I also submerged the socks in water to compare how well they kept moisture out and how they performed after getting thoroughly wet.

I evaluated each pair for waterproofing, fit, comfort, breathability, durability, and drying performance. I also paid attention to sock height and cuff design, since keeping water from entering through the top can matter just as much as the waterproof membrane itself.

Top Pick: The Sealskinz Dunton Waterproof All Weather Ankle Length Sock with Hydrostop is our Best Overall waterproof sock. It kept my feet dry during steady-rain hiking, dried quickly, and has a secure Hydrostop cuff that helped prevent water from running into the sock from above. It’s lighter and less cushioned than some of the thicker options I tested, but it offered the best overall balance of waterproof protection, fit, breathability, and durability.

If you’re interested in warm, wool socks for cold weather, check out our Best Winter Socks guide.

