By far the most comfortable of the waterproof socks we tested, the Bridgedale StormSock is an ideal pick if you’re a hiker, biker, or camper looking for a reliable pair of waterproof socks. We put these socks to the test on a 70-mile bike ride in a continuous downpour, and on casual hikes in the Midwest rainy season. Their wide fit around the ankle, superior room in the toe and arch of the foot, and added cushion throughout won us over.

The most comfortable, cushioned high-performance waterproof sock of our testing pool, the Bridgedale StormSock rose to the top of the list for our go-to pick for all outdoor activities.

