Best Men’s Walking Shoes of 2026

Comfortable, supportive men's shoes for travel, fitness, work, and all-day wear

October 6th, 2026Home → Gear Reviews → Footwear

Anyone who has ever walked a mile in ill-fitting, unsupportive, or generally uncomfortable shoes knows how important a quality pair of walking shoes is, especially if you’ll be on your feet all day. A pair that feels fine taking out the trash can turn into heel rubbing a couple of hours into a work shift or arch fatigue while hurrying to catch your layover flight.

We tested the top walking shoes and tracked performance for over a year, from icy sidewalks in January to scorching pavement in July, to help you prevent those aforementioned discomforts. We wore them on daily commutes, errands, travel days, and up to 12-hour hospital shifts on our feet. We tested comparable models side by side to see how cushioning and support actually held up against each other, rather than just against a spec sheet.

We paid close attention to whether the cushioning packed out, whether the fit stayed secure, whether new hot spots formed, and how well the sole gripped on wet, slick tile and trails. We also factored in style and how easily the shoes transitioned between activities, since many people don't want to swap shoes between work and happy hour, workouts, or errands.

Top Pick: The HOKA Bondi SR earns our Best Overall award. It remained cushioned and comfortable through 7-hour brewery shifts and 12-hour nursing shifts. It gripped equally well on wet tile and dry pavement during testing, carries the American Podiatric Medical Association Seal of Acceptance, and is stylish and functional enough to transition from work to walks.

