Many runners and hikers that wear running shoes or hiking sandals during the summer find traditional winter hiking boots to be uncomfortable. At the request of readers, we searched for a comfortable winter boot.

The most comfortable winter boots we found are the Lems Chelsea Barefoot Waterproof. With a wide toe box and leather uppers that wear to the shape of your feet, our testers consistently reach for these over other winter boots.

The Lems Chelsea Barefoot Waterproof Boots are stylish, easy to slip on and comfortable for people with wide feet or who just want their toes to spread out. It's lined with a waterproof membrane and has a lot of flexibility while also providing a sturdier midsole than some other minimalist shoes.

